.TH MONGOOSE-CLIENT 1 "September 2026" "mongoose-j2534 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mongoose-client \- exercise the MongoosePro J2534 library from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mongoose-client
[\fBserial:\fISERIAL\fR]
.B \-\-script
.I FILE
[\fB\-\-gap\fR \fIMS\fR]
.br
.B mongoose-client
.B \-\-script\-check
.IR FILE ...
.br
.B mongoose-client
[\fBserial:\fISERIAL\fR]
.I MODE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mongoose-client
links the J2534 library directly and drives it, so what it does is what an application using
.BR libmongoose_j2534 (7)
would do. It is a test and validation tool, not a diagnostic application.
.PP
.B Use it at your own risk.
It sends messages to a vehicle's networks. The
.B \-\-vehicle\-*
modes and the bundled scripts send read-only OBD-II requests (a few change a channel setting and restore it), but
.B \-\-script
runs whatever script it is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-script " FILE"
Run a step file, one J2534 call per line (see
.IR tools/scripts/README.md ).
The same files run on the Windows reference harness, and both print the same log lines, so a run on each can be
compared after removing the
.B utc_100ns=
timestamps. Exit status 1 if a step failed. A malformed number or hex string exits with 2.
.TP
.BI \-\-gap " MS"
Sleep this many milliseconds after each step.
.TP
.BI \-\-script\-check " FILE" ...
Parse each script and validate every step without touching an adapter. This is what the
.B script_syntax
test runs.
.SS Vehicle modes
All of these connect at 500 kbit and send only read-only requests.
.TP
.B \-\-vehicle\-listen
Listen on a raw CAN channel with a wildcard filter for a few seconds. Transmits nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-vehicle\-check
Listen, then send mode 01 PID 00 and mode 09 PID 02 to 0x7DF on a raw CAN channel and report the replies.
.TP
.B \-\-vehicle\-iso
The same VIN request on an ISO15765 channel, showing the reassembled multi-frame reply.
.TP
.B \-\-vehicle\-soak
Five minutes of passive receive with a wildcard filter; reports rate, timestamp gaps and overflows.
.TP
.B \-\-vehicle\-cycles
100 full open, connect, request, disconnect, close cycles on an ISO15765 channel. Stops at the first failure.
.TP
.B \-\-vehicle\-cycles\-raw
The same on a raw CAN channel.
.TP
.B \-\-vehicle\-hour
One hour on a raw CAN channel: continuous receive plus one mode 01 request a second.
.TP
.B \-\-vehicle\-hour\-iso
One hour on an ISO15765 channel: a functional request each second, and mode 09 PID 04 every tenth second.
.TP
.B \-\-vehicle\-ignition
A passive observer for switching the ignition off and on: one line a second of frame rate, bus state and battery
voltage. It sends a mode 01 request every ten seconds only while frames arrive, and stops after two go unanswered.
.SS Bench modes
.TP
.B \-\-can\-lifecycle, \-\-can\-receive\-check, \-\-can\-transmit\-check
Bench checks that also connect at 250 kbit. Do not use them on a vehicle at 500 kbit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MONGOOSE_SOAK_SECONDS
Duration of
.B \-\-vehicle\-hour
and
.B \-\-vehicle\-hour\-iso
(default 3600).
.TP
.B MONGOOSE_OBSERVE_SECONDS
Duration of
.B \-\-vehicle\-ignition
(default 600).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if a check or a script step failed; 2 for a usage error or an unreadable script.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I tools/scripts/*.txt
The step files. The ones named
.B \-expectfail
are expected to exit 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mongoose-diag (1),
.BR libmongoose_j2534 (7)
